Thomas


00:00:01,420 --> 00:00:07,680 [speaker_0]
Hi, thanks for participating this interview with me today. This should take about five to 10 minutes. Are you okay with me recording this?

00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:08,370 [speaker_1]
Yep, that's fine.

00:00:08,380 --> 00:00:16,239 [speaker_0]
Okay. Um, so let's begin with the first question. So what usually stops you from approaching or talking to new people at uni?

00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:23,880 [speaker_1]
I think just the environment and just the intimidating nature of doing it. Um, it's obviously quite a big place, and there's lots of people from different ethnicities, age groups, so it's always a bit of an intimidating thing to do.

00:00:38,400 --> 00:00:47,000 [speaker_0]
Okay. Um, and what has helped you so far, um, and what has helped you the most in building a network of friends?

00:00:47,940 --> 00:00:54,360 [speaker_1]
Having, um, a third place like the bar at the uni is always good. Um, you can meet a lot of people there who share similar interests. Um, it's a place you can also hang out, um, with people that you meet from class as well, ... you might have made in class.

00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:17,760 [speaker_0]
So would you, like, go there after class to the Red Room-

00:01:18,360 --> 00:01:19,140 [speaker_1]
Yeah, we'd have a- ... uh, like a chat in class, and then if we had some free time, we'd go there- ... and, uh, yeah, swap socials or something.

00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:33,040 [speaker_0]
Mm-hmm. Um, and what do you think makes it hard to approach other students?

00:01:35,240 --> 00:01:53,460 [speaker_1]
Um, I'd have to just say, you know, it's, it's an unfamiliar place. You've never met them before. You don't even know... You don't know anything about them. … it's not like school, where you're all familiar. They're just complete strangers, essentially.

00:01:58,600 --> 00:02:06,980 [speaker_0]
Okay. Um, and what do you think would make it easier for you to build friendships or find community at uni?

00:02:09,220 --> 00:02:33,210 [speaker_1]
Um, joining clubs, whether, um, you all have similar interests, or going to certain events, um, or facilities, um, where there's like-minded people, so you have that commonality to bounce off and build off a friendship from there.

00:02:33,480 --> 00:02:42,400 [speaker_0]
Okay. And what do you think is lacking from finding friends via, like, clubs or university events?

00:02:43,840 --> 00:02:44,440 [speaker_1]
What's missing?

00:02:44,680 --> 00:02:49,600 [speaker_0]
Yeah, what's... Yeah, what's lacking from the current setup with clubs and uni events, do you reckon?

00:02:51,700 --> 00:03:06,940 [speaker_1]
Um, I guess the variety of clubs. There's not always, um... You know, there's clubs that don't really interest me. Um, so- ... I'd like to see maybe more variety of clubs- ... that I would, uh, like to join.

00:03:12,720 --> 00:03:20,100 [speaker_0]
Have you ever struggled with, um, clubs, like, making times that don't suit your, like, schedule?

00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:23,660 [speaker_1]
In... What do you mean?

00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:29,190 [speaker_0]
Um, as in, like, when they're organizing events, do they sometimes not align with your schedule?

00:03:29,220 --> 00:03:43,940 [speaker_1]
Yeah, that... I guess that also makes it, um, hard. And because it's, you're living off campus, um, you're usually having to do these events to meet people in your own time- ... which also kind of makes it another barrier to, to sort of entry-

00:03:51,520 --> 00:03:56,840 [speaker_0]
Um, and would you prefer connecting with someone one-on-one or in a group setting?

00:03:57,640 --> 00:04:03,180 [speaker_1]
I think initially a group setting, and then once you become more comfortable with them, that one-on-one- ... is probably, um, a good one.

00:04:06,400 --> 00:04:08,480 [speaker_0]
And why do you think initially a group setting?

00:04:09,520 --> 00:04:21,040 [speaker_1]
Um, because I think just with anyone it can be a bit awkward, and you don't know, you know, all of their likes and interests, so you can just initially bounce off each other. Um, reflect that way. And then once you're comfortable, you've broken that ice, you can then have a more meaningful one-on-one chat, because I guess you're more comfortable in each other's... um, space.

00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:42,700 [speaker_0]
Okay. Um, and before you get to know someone or connect with someone, what kind of information do you think you'd want to know about them?

00:04:43,860 --> 00:04:56,490 [speaker_1]
Um, their age, where they grew up, their interests, hobbies. Um, if they play games, if they're sporty- ... what sports they like, if they, um, watch sports. All that sort of stuff.

00:05:02,040 --> 00:05:09,480 [speaker_0]
Okay. Um, and have you ever used any apps, group chats, or platforms to connect with people?

00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:16,800 [speaker_1]
Um, no. It's all just been in person.

00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:22,080 [speaker_0]
Okay. And what... Why do you think is the reason that you haven't been drawn to any of these apps?

00:05:22,980 --> 00:05:30,180 [speaker_1]
Um, I'm not really aware of... I've been aware of many apps like that in the first place, I guess.

00:05:31,340 --> 00:05:33,360 [speaker_0]
So do you think they need more, like, publicity?

00:05:34,280 --> 00:05:35,160 [speaker_1]
Yeah. Yeah. And just, um... Yeah, I think publicity's a, a good starting point.

00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:50,520 [speaker_0]
Yeah. Um, and if you were to design an app to help you make friends, what features would you be looking for, um, in this app, and why?

00:05:51,700 --> 00:05:57,920 [speaker_1]
Um, an emphasis on unis, specifically UQ. Um, not making it too sort of general, but more specific to Australian or Queensland unis. Um, and an emphasis, yeah, on, like, profiles, meetups, um, events, like being able to host events. Um, and then having interests and commonalities on profiles that you can sort of view ... as well.

00:06:30,720 --> 00:06:38,240 [speaker_0]
Um, and then final question: What would you… What would make you feel comfortable reaching out to someone new through an app?

00:06:40,220 --> 00:06:43,220 [speaker_1]
Um, what do you mean? Like-

00:06:43,920 --> 00:06:47,120 [speaker_0]
Like, what would make it easier for you to reach out to someone?

00:06:49,060 --> 00:06:55,640 [speaker_1]
If, say, we had the same... We're in the same age group- ... and had some similar interests and were both at uni-... I think that would be a pretty good start.

00:07:06,240 --> 00:07:11,300 [speaker_0]
All right, cool. That's all the questions I had for today. Thank you very much for participating.

00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:11,640 [speaker_1]
Thank you.
